---
import Header from '@/components/common/header/Header.astro';
import Layout, { type Props } from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/common/Footer.astro';
import PrivacyWrapper from '@/components/privacy/PrivacyWrapper.astro';

import { baseMetaData } from '@/helpers/SEO';
import { DEFAULT_LOCALE, type Locale } from '@/config/i18n';

const currentLocale = (Astro.currentLocale as Locale) || DEFAULT_LOCALE;

const baseMeta = baseMetaData[currentLocale] || baseMetaData.en;

const metadata: Props['metadata'] = {
  ...baseMeta,
  title: `Privacy Policy - ${baseMeta.title}`,
  lang: currentLocale,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Header />

  <PrivacyWrapper firstTitle='Privacy' secondTitle='Policy'>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 26, 2025</p>
    <p>
      At <strong>Fusion Tower</strong>, we are committed to protecting the
      privacy and security of the personal data of our users, prospective
      clients, and visitors to our website (www.fusiontower.net).
    </p>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, store, share, and
      protect the personal information you provide when interacting with our
      Site and our professional services.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy has been developed to comply with applicable regulations,
      including Law 1581 of 2012 and Decree 1377 of 2013 of the Republic of
      Colombia, as well as applicable privacy regulations in the United States.
    </p>
    <p>
      By using our Site or voluntarily providing us with your information, you
      agree to the practices described in this policy and expressly consent to
      the processing of your personal data in accordance with the terms set
      forth herein.
    </p>
    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>
      The party responsible for the processing of personal data collected
      through this Site is Fusion Tower. For any matter related to the privacy
      of your data, you may contact us via email at: <a
        href='mailto:alex@fusiontower.net'>alex@fusiontower.net</a
      >.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect two types of information from users of our Site:</p>
    <h3>2.1. Personally Identifiable Information (PII)</h3>
    <p>
      This is information that you voluntarily provide to us that allows you to
      be identified directly or indirectly. This occurs primarily when you use
      our contact forms (such as "Let's Talk About Your Project"), request
      information about services, or subscribe to newsletters. The PII we may
      collect includes, but is not limited to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full name.</li>
      <li>Corporate or personal email address.</li>
      <li>Phone number.</li>
      <li>Name of the company or organization you represent.</li>
      <li>Details about your project or business needs.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2.2. Non-Personal Information and Navigation Data</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, we automatically collect certain technical information
      when you visit our Site. This information does not directly identify you
      personally but is useful for improving your experience and analyzing Site
      performance. This may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP Address.</li>
      <li>Browser type and version.</li>
      <li>Device operating system.</li>
      <li>Pages visited within our Site and duration of the visit.</li>
      <li>
        Data collected through cookies and similar technologies (see Section 6).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>3. Purpose of Data Processing</h2>
    <p>
      We use the collected information for the following legitimate business
      purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service Provision and Customer Support:</strong> To respond to your
        inquiries sent through contact forms, analyze your project needs, and provide
        you with proposals for consulting, strategy, and technology development services.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Commercial Communications:</strong> With your prior and express consent,
        we may send you information about our services, updates, articles of interest,
        and news about Fusion Tower that we consider relevant to your business. You
        may opt out of receiving these communications at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Website Improvement:</strong> To analyze usage trends, administer
        the Site, and enhance its functionality and security.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal Compliance:</strong> To comply with applicable legal, regulatory,
        and fiscal obligations in Colombia and the United States.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
    <p>The processing of your personal data is based on:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Consent:</strong> By submitting your data through our contact
        forms, you grant your free, prior, express, and informed consent for Fusion
        Tower to treat your data in accordance with this policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate Interest:</strong> To ensure the security of our website
        and improve our B2B (Business-to-Business) services.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Performance of a Contract:</strong> If you contract our services,
        processing will be necessary for the execution of the commercial relationship.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>5. Sharing and Transferring Information</h2>
    <p>
      Fusion Tower does not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to
      third parties for their promotional purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, we may share your information in the following limited
      circumstances:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service Providers:</strong> With trusted third parties who provide
        services necessary to operate our business (for example, web hosting providers,
        email services, Customer Relationship Management - CRM tools). These third
        parties are prohibited from using your personal data for purposes other than
        those contracted and are obligated to maintain confidentiality.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> If we are required to do so by law or
        if we believe in good faith that such action is necessary to comply with a
        legal proceeding, court order, or legal process.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>International Data Transfer:</strong> Given that Fusion Tower operates
        with clients and resources in Colombia and the United States, your information
        may be transferred to, stored, and processed on servers located outside your
        country of residence. By providing your data, you consent to this international
        transfer. We ensure that such transfers are performed under adequate levels
        of protection and information security.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>6. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Our Site uses "cookies" and similar technologies to enhance the user
      experience and analyze traffic. A cookie is a small text file stored on
      your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can configure your browser to reject all cookies or to indicate when a
      cookie is being sent. However, if you do not accept cookies, some parts of
      our Site may not function properly.
    </p>
    <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We implement reasonable and appropriate technical, administrative, and
      physical security measures to protect the personal information we collect
      from unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. However,
      please note that no method of transmission over the Internet or method of
      electronic storage is 100% secure.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Your Rights as a Data Subject</h2>
    <p>
      In accordance with applicable regulations (including the Habeas Data
      regime in Colombia), you have the following rights regarding your personal
      data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Access:</strong> To know what personal data of yours we are processing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Update and Rectification:</strong> To request the correction of inaccurate,
        incomplete, or outdated data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deletion (Cancellation):</strong> To request the deletion of your
        personal data from our databases when there is no legal or contractual duty
        to maintain them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Revocation of Consent:</strong> To revoke the authorization granted
        for the processing of your data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Opposition:</strong> To oppose the processing of your data for specific
        purposes.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, please send a written request to the
      email address <a href='mailto:alex@fusiontower.net'
        >alex@fusiontower.net</a
      >, detailing your request and fully identifying yourself.
    </p>
    <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our Site and our services are directed exclusively to businesses and
      professionals (B2B environment). We do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children under the age of 18. If you are a parent or
      guardian and believe that your child has provided us with personal
      information, please contact us so we can delete such information.
    </p>
    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      Fusion Tower reserves the right to update or modify this Privacy Policy at
      any time to reflect changes in our practices or legal regulations. Any
      changes will be published on this page, and the "Last updated" date at the
      top will be revised. We recommend reviewing this policy periodically.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, concerns, or comments about this Privacy Policy or
      how we handle your personal data, please contact us at:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Fusion Tower</strong><br />
      Email: <a href='mailto:alex@fusiontower.net'>alex@fusiontower.net</a>
    </p>
  </PrivacyWrapper>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
